    ],
    ":question/id": "0a9e6824-677a-5fae-9867-1701e7d8378f",
    ":question/math-academy-id": "e-4697",
    ":question/problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n![](images/46/464ba24026d89efb3e62f7807426e5c413f277da3c8087931d2e3fde9a0b8e74.svg)\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system represented by the matrix.",
    ":question/worked-solution": "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & -8\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -8\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{8}{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n![](images/ba/baf05a693deacc3ef644165bae4de7b1435a90c73f050ac76c48892b2e010393.svg)\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=1$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+2(1)=0 \n\t\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad\n\tx=-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-2$ and $y=1.$ Or, in vector form, $\\left<  -2,1 \\right>.$"
  },
